    "evidence_text": "We describe our system and innovations, as well as comparing our results to a Naive Bayes baseline.\n\n- ?`Cobra?\n\n- Does it charge?\n\nThus, building a system to classify the humor of tweets is a difficult task.\n\nal.\n\nExamples and data can be found on the CodaLab competition webpage.\n\nThe primary steps are: Below we will give more detail on each step and the parameters used to generate our system.\n\nWe excluded retweets to minimize repeated examples in our language model training.\n\nAdd spaces between special chars (ie.\n\nVamos por mas!!!\n\nFor the LM, we selected an ASGD Weight-Dropped Long\n\nWe tied the embedding weights  on the encoder and decoder for training.\n\nWe thus chose to use QRNN units due to improved training speed compared to the alternatives.\n\nThis model has about 60 million trainable parameters.\n\nFor all networks we applied a dropout multiplier which scales the dropout used throughout the network.\n\nWe used the Adam optimizer with weight decay as indicated in the table.\n\nThis largest weight is shown in Table TABREF21 under \"Learning Rate.\"\n\nSubsequent training epochs were run with one-cycle and lower learning rates\n\nWe layout our training parameters in Table TABREF25 .\n\nFrom these samples, we select the best validation F1 metric or Mean Squared Error (MSE) for use in our test submission.\n\nWe add a hidden layer and linear output head and MSE loss function.\n\nThis initialization affects the final F1 metric achievable.\n\nWe selected our single best random seed for the test submission.\n\nWith more exploration, a better seed could likely be found.\n\npre-training, and further select the best down-stream seed similar to Czapla et al  .\n\nThe first is the baseline NBSVM solution, with an F1 of 0.7548.\n\nThis produced our final submission of 0.8099.\n\nOur solution placed\n\nWe describe the data collection, pre-training, and final model building steps for this contest.\n\nAuthor Contributions\tBF was the primary researcher.\n\nAlso, Kyle Kastner for his edits, suggestions and recommendations in writing up these results.",
